Some of you might remember the Log Analyzer I created with Visual Basic
few years back. Well, it wasn't that successful a project, I admit.
I've now taken it down for good and replaced it with an online version.
The analyzer can be found from my Illustrated NetHack Monsters page at
http://koti.mbnet.fi/villes/nethack/illustrated_nethack.php

It works in a simple manner: you type your name (or nickname), find the
record or logfile from your NetHack directory and click Submit. No file
is saved on the server, so you will need to manually save the resulting
xhtml-document and, should you want to share it with others, come up
with some web space somewhere.

I thought this would help offline players get the same kind of nifty
statistics from their games as most online servers already provide. I
know there are already a few log analyzers, but they seem to be made
with Perl or in something similar language that is native to
*nix-systems. One good side in my online log analyzer is that it works
on all operating systems provided that you have a web browser and an
internet connection, which most of you probably do as you are reading
this post. ;) I'm looking forward to hear some comments or suggestions.

